00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:38.760
Now, to really understand the Bolivia story, most coverage of emergency declarations assumed they

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:45.520
are short-term, narrowly tailored responses to immediate threats. In practice, the legal framework

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:51.400
in many countries allows leaders to bypass normal legislative checks, redirect budgets,

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:57.840
and limit public assembly with limited, immediate oversight. Historical examples from Latin America

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:03.700
show that once invoked, these powers can remain in place for months while courts review challenges

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:09.840
slowly. Knowing this, when you hear officials describe an emergency as temporary and proportionate,

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:14.980
you can check whether prior declarations in the same country were later extended or broadened.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:20.720
Next time you see a headline about a state of emergency, ask what exact statutes are being used,

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:26.800
